nodeFrideApprovedNote
	⚠️ That includes fride. fride lets fridolin hand coding tasks to FrIDE on this machine. FrIDE runs Claude Code agents there, and they can run anything this machine's user can (on Windows through WSL, PowerShell and C:\ too), whatever exec allows or refuses: approving fride is approving arbitrary commands on this machine. Approve it only on a machine you would let fridolin do anything on. `!revoke <id>` takes it back.
nodeRevokedCoreSecretsNote
	🔐 It is a core host, and forgot what moves brought it first:
	• host secrets: CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
	• the core's data dir: bridge.db, config.json
nodeRevokedCoreSecretsNote(none)
	🔐 It is a core host; it held nothing a move brought it.
nodeRevokedCoreSecretsNote(failed)
	🔐 It is a core host and could not forget what moves brought it first (it is offline). If it held host secrets, rotate them: docs/CORE.md, "A core host that is gone".
